.TH LIBHEARTBEAT_SENDER_LIB 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
libheartbeat_sender_lib \- C++ heartbeat sender library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <heartbeat_sender_lib.h>
.PP
.B namespace hbsender {
.B struct Config {
.B "    std::string name;"
.B "    std::string status   = \(dqOK\(dq;"
.B "    std::string host     = \(dq127.0.0.1\(dq;"
.B "    int         port     = 9999;"
.B "    double      interval = 0.0;"
.B "    int         count    = 0;"
.B "    std::string iface;"
.B "    bool        verbose  = false;"
.B };
.PP
.BI "std::string now_iso8601();"
.BI "std::string build_packet(const std::string& " name ", const std::string& " status );
.BI "void send_packet(const std::string& " host ", int " port ","
.BI "                 const std::string& " data ", const std::string& " iface );
.BI "void load_json_file(const std::string& " path ", Config& " cfg );
.B }
.fi
.PP
Link with
.B heartbeat_sender_lib
(static,
.IR libheartbeat_sender_lib.a )
and
.BR nlohmann_json::nlohmann_json .
.SH DESCRIPTION
A small static library for emitting heartbeats understood by
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1).
It is the core of
.BR heartbeat_sender (1)
and can be linked into any C++17 DAQ process that should report liveness.
.TP
.B now_iso8601()
Current UTC time as
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmm+00:00 .
.TP
.B build_packet()
Returns the compact JSON object
.B {\(dqname\(dq:...,\(dqtimestamp\(dq:...,\(dqstatus\(dq:...}
with
.I name
and
.I status
JSON\-escaped (short escapes for
.BR \e\(dq ,
.BR \e\e ,
.BR \eb ,
.BR \ef ,
.BR \en ,
.BR \er ,
.BR \et ;
other bytes below 0x20 as
.BR \eu00XX ;
everything else, including UTF\-8, passed through unchanged).
.TP
.B send_packet()
Sends
.I data
as one UDP datagram.
A
.BI % iface
suffix on
.I host
is stripped and used as the interface when
.I iface
is empty.
An IPv4 literal is sent with
.B SO_BROADCAST
set, or with a multicast TTL of 32 if it is a multicast group.
An IPv6 literal is sent with a multicast hop limit of 32 and
.B IPV6_MULTICAST_IF
for multicast groups; link\-local unicast
.RI ( fe80::/10 )
and link\-local multicast
.RI ( ff02::/16 )
require an interface.
Anything else is resolved with
.BR getaddrinfo (3)
and sent to the first result.
.TP
.B load_json_file()
Fills the fields of
.I cfg
present in the JSON object at
.IR path .
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B send_packet()
and
.B load_json_file()
return nothing and report failure by throwing.
.SH ERRORS
.B std::runtime_error
is thrown for: socket creation failure;
.BR sendto (2)
failure on an IP literal; an unknown interface name; a link\-local destination
without an interface; an unresolvable host name; an unreadable or invalid JSON
file.
A
.BR sendto (2)
failure on the host\-name path is not detected.
.BR load_json_file()
can also throw
.B nlohmann::json::type_error
when a key has the wrong JSON type.
.SH NOTES
POSIX sockets only; the library does not build on Windows.
No CMake package configuration is exported; consume it with
.B add_subdirectory(cpp_sender)
or by pointing at the installed header and archive.
Install locations:
.I include/heartbeat_sender_lib.h
and
.IR lib/libheartbeat_sender_lib.a .
The test suite is
.I cpp_sender/tests/test_heartbeat_sender_lib.cpp
(20 GoogleTest cases).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <heartbeat_sender_lib.h>

void beat() {
    std::string p = hbsender::build_packet("daq\-node\-01", "OK");
    hbsender::send_packet("monitor\-host", 9999, p, "");
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_sender (1),
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
